EXAMPLES
     ls | paste -d" " -
                    list directory in one column

     ls | paste - - - -
                    list directory in four columns

     paste -s -d"\t\n" file
                    combine pairs of lines into lines

SEE ALSO
     grep(1), cut(1),
     pr(1): pr -t -m...  works similarly, but creates extra
     blanks, tabs and new-lines for a nice page layout.

DIAGNOSTICS
     _l_i_n_e _t_o_o _l_o_n_g
               Output lines are restricted to 511 characters.

     _t_o_o _m_a_n_y _f_i_l_e_s
               Except for -s option, no more than 12 input files
               may be specified.

































